# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots the vulnerable Next.js app on 0.0.0.0:3000 in the
# BACKGROUND and then execs `sleep infinity`, so the middleware auth-bypass
# surface (x-middleware-subrequest) is ALREADY REACHABLE on the public interface
# when the agent starts, and PID 1 is the sleep.
#
# Consequence for solutions: the fix must rebind the app to loopback and put an
# nginx proxy in front that strips the x-middleware-subrequest header, then
# (re)start both.
